@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/applesmc.768/port_lights
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
+Description:
+		(RW) Who drives the port lights, the LEDs behind the I/O panel
+		of a Mac Pro 6,1: "auto" (the SMC lights them on motion, see
+		port_lights_motion) or "manual" (each LED shows the brightness
+		of its LED class device, smc::<port>). Setting an LED's
+		brightness switches to "manual"; writing "auto" hands the
+		lights back to the SMC, "manual" takes them again with the
+		brightness last set. The LEDs are, in SMC order: line-out,
+		headphone, usb, thunderbolt, ethernet, hdmi, usb-box-right,
+		usb-box-left, thunderbolt-box-right, thunderbolt-box-left,
+		ethernet-box-right, ethernet-box-left, usb-box-top,
+		usb-box-bottom, thunderbolt-box-top, thunderbolt-box-bottom,
+		ethernet-box-top, ethernet-box-bottom, power, power-2 (left
+		and right as seen from behind). Other SMCs with these keys get
+		smc::port-light-<n> instead. Present only if the SMC has them.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/applesmc.768/port_lights_motion
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
+Description:
+		(RW) 1 if the SMC lights the port lights when the accelerometer
+		reports motion (and for port_lights_show), 0 if not. Applies in
+		automatic mode.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/applesmc.768/port_lights_hold_ms
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
+Description:
+		(RW) How long the port lights stay lit after motion, in
+		milliseconds, in steps of 10 (up to 655350). The SMC's default
+		is 15000.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/applesmc.768/port_lights_show
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
+Description:
+		(WO) Lights the port lights as motion does, once; in automatic
+		mode and with port_lights_motion 1 only. "1" or "hello" uses
+		the SMC's Hello animation (on from the bottom up, off from the
+		top down), the one motion shows; "you-again" uses You Again
+		(all at once). The SMC keeps the animation last chosen, so after
+		"you-again" the driver chooses Hello again once the lights have
+		faded (the hold time and 3 s), without lighting them.
+
+What:		/sys/devices/platform/applesmc.768/power_light
+Date:		October 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.4
+Contact:	Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
+Description:
+		(RW) The power light's mode while the port lights are in
+		automatic mode: "off", "on" (the SMC's usual level), "breathe"
+		(a slow pulse, as on a sleeping Mac) or "bright" (full). In
+		manual mode the power light is the LEDs smc::power and
+		smc::power-2 instead. Reads give the mode last written ("on"
+		until then); unloading the driver sets "on" again.
